// What a render-time filter must look at on one element, decided once.
//
// A LEAF that imports nothing of tutuca's — only what `derive(Debug)` pulls in —
// and that is its whole reason to exist. The fact it carries is produced by
// `render` (which walks anode's attributes) and
// consumed by `vdom/filter` (whose rules read it), and those two packages
// deliberately cannot name a type in each other's:
//
// - `vdom/filter` is "over `vdom` and nothing else" — importing `anode` there
//   would put a template compiler behind every render, which is the reason
//   `handler.mbt` duplicates a two-line prefix test rather than importing it.
// - `anode` is imported by everything, so a type it holds must cost nothing;
//   the name tables that DECIDE these bits sit behind a CSS tokenizer and an
//   HTML parser, and neither belongs in every consumer of the view tree.
//
// So the type is here, alone, and the tables stay where they are. Same shape of
// argument as `anode/sanitize/css`'s header, for the same reason: a fact three
// packages share can only live somewhere none of them owns.
